# Plan: design artifacts

Use only after design level is confirmed.

Explain why selected depth is proportionate and weaker/stronger levels are insufficient or Not needed. `none` records rationale/risks; lightweight uses `design-overview`; HLD and LLD use their matching kinds; GDD is game-only and follows game domain skills. Canonical design Markdown lives only under `.harnessctl/documents`.

Reuse an artifact only after bounded `document_list` discovery and `document_get` checks relevance, status, version, and current revision. Before create/revise, show kind, purpose, scope, canonical path, parent, and link target; confirm action. Create v1 as `draft` with `document_create` and content without an H1. Use `document_update` for same-version review corrections and `document_version` for a semantic successor; preserve prior versions. Separately confirm the transition to `review`, obtain a fresh exact revision with `document_get`, then mutate with that `expectedRevision`. After review, separately confirm the transition to `approved`, obtain another fresh exact revision immediately before mutation, and use only that revision. Link only the approved active canonical path with separately confirmed `issue_link_document`. Run both `document_validate` and `issue_validate` after linking and before checkpointing. HLD+LLD follows dependency order. Never edit managed frontmatter/path state directly or copy artifact bodies into issues or memory.
